// Zed keymap — stowed to ~/.config/zed/keymap.json (see README → "Zed").
// Vim-mode leader layer carried over from nvim: the "borrow" rows of
// docs/zed-vim-keymap.md (the "try" rows, alt-h/j/k/l resize and ctrl-\
// terminal, are left out). nvim keymaps live in GUIDE.md.
//
// Vim block (added 2026-11-22, untested; COMMENTED OUT below, uncomment the
// entries to adopt): risks and rows to reconsider.
// - space is now a chord prefix: plain space (move right) waits out the chord
//   timeout (1 s) before firing alone. y p / y u / y shift-p add no delay to
//   y y or y i w (y resolves on the next key, as an operator does anyway).
// - H / L are not bound (you don't use them for tabs), so they stay vim's
//   WindowTop / WindowBottom. Tabs: [b / ]b, cmd-{ / cmd-}.
//   g b is NOT bound either (it stays Zed's block-comment toggle); use ctrl-^
//   for the alternate file.
// - ctrl-h/j/k/l change meaning in normal mode (backspace, down, kill-ring
//   cut, scroll-center). The Dock block is "Dock && !Terminal", so a docked
//   terminal keeps readline keys but ctrl-h/j/k/l can't leave it: use f6
//   (cmd-k clears a terminal, so cmd-k chords never fire there).
// - The !Editor block skips ProjectPanel/GitPanel/OutlinePanel (they bind
//   plain space), so space e / g g / a a don't work from those panels.
// - space a l (thread switcher) is a hold-the-modifier popup; from a chord it
//   may stay open until Enter or Esc. space a d does nothing without an active
//   agent conversation. space a n / l / v need the agent UI enabled.
// - Git prefix is space g *, but nvim's diffview keys are <leader>v*. Pick one
//   after a week (see docs/zed-vim-keymap.md, "To check").
// - Verified against v1.29.2 and the ~/src/zed nightly (2026-11-19), not the
//   installed 1.29.3: re-check an action name if a binding does nothing
//   (dev: open key context view).
//
// Staged groups, with a verdict on each (usage unmeasured; cross out what you
// never press). Keep = real gap in Zed; Optional = Zed already has a key;
// Cheap = low cost either way.
// - Panes and tabs: ctrl-h/j/k/l, space space, space b b/x/o
//   Keep ctrl-h/j/k/l (+ Dock block): docks aren't panes, so ctrl-w h/j/k/l
//   dead-ends at panels. space space = cmd-p; space b b/x/o = ctrl-tab,
//   cmd-w, alt-cmd-t: Optional.
// - Search: space s f/g/w/s/d/r/k
//   Optional: cmd-p, cmd-shift-f, gS, gs, cmd-k cmd-p, cmd-k cmd-s exist.
//   Keep only if the leader reflex is strong.
// - Peek: space p d/t/i/r
//   Keep if you use nvim's peek floats; gd/gy/gri/grr give the multibuffer
//   version, and ctrl-w d / ctrl-w D already open the picker.
// - Code: space c a/f/d, space t i
//   Optional: gra / g. (code action), cmd-shift-i (format), cmd-shift-m
//   (diagnostics). ctrl-: for inlay hints is a stretch, so space t i is Keep.
// - Panels: space e, space o
//   Keep space e (reveal in tree); space o = cmd-shift-b. Neither works from
//   inside the panels themselves (excluded contexts).
// - Git: space g g/d/p/c/f, space t b
//   Keep space g d/p/c/f and space t b (no default key). space g g has f6 /
//   the palette as the alternative. Prefix is g here, v in nvim: decide.
// - Agent: space a a/x/n/l/v/d, visual space a t/s
//   Optional: space a a = cmd-?; space a x = ctrl-alt-w. space a l is the
//   shakiest (popup may stay open); space a d needs an active thread.
//   space a n/v/d have no easy default key.
// - Debugger: space d b/c/i/o/O/q/l/u
//   Optional: the F-keys match nvim's. Keep only for away-from-F-row use.
// - Toggles and yanks: space t n/d, y p/P/u
//   Keep y p/P/u (copy path, permalink: no useful default); space t n/d are
//   rarely pressed. y becomes a chord prefix (no delay for y y / y i w).
// - Insert: jk
//   Cheap and a strong reflex if you use it in nvim; skip if you reach for
//   escape.
[
    // Swap the floating text finder and editable project-search tab shortcuts.
    // Unscoped bindings override the defaults in editors and search bars alike.
    {
        "use_key_equivalents": true,
        "bindings": {
            "cmd-shift-f": "text_finder::Toggle",
            "alt-cmd-f": "pane::DeploySearch"
        }
    },
    // Step through agent threads in sidebar order. Zed has no default key for
    // this; ctrl-tab opens the MRU switcher instead. Scoped to the agent panel
    // and threads sidebar so alt-] / alt-[ still type normally in editors.
    {
        "context": "AgentPanel || ThreadsSidebar",
        "bindings": {
            "alt-]": "multi_workspace::NextThread",
            "alt-[": "multi_workspace::PreviousThread"
        }
    },
